Sval: Mozilla's tests load other pages where they loaded pages Sval removes

Sval does not build about:robots or about:firefoxview
(no-closed-about-pages.patch), so a test that opens one as an arbitrary page
gets an error page in its place. A test that wants a page in the parent process, as about:robots
is, loads about:license, which Sval keeps open for the notices it shows; the
others load a page of the harness's server. A test file has no chrome API to
change the page it names, so the tests are patched.

